===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|theology|transitive|intransitive}} To [[condemn]].
#: {{ux|en|The official position is that anyone who does this will be '''damned''' for all eternity.}}
#: {{ux|en|Only God can '''damn'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|I '''damn''' you eternally, fiend!}}
# To condemn; to declare guilty; to doom; to adjudge to punishment.
#: {{syn|en|convict|doom}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Julius Caesar|IV|i|passage=He shall not live; look, with a spot I '''damn''' him.}}
#* {{RQ:Time|title='What I Learned From Adopting Two Children With Rare Genetic Conditions'|author=Stephanie Sinclair|date=May 12 2018|text=Lack of access to support services can '''damn''' children with disabilities and lesser means to lives where they never harness their full range of abilities.|url=https://time.com/longform/adoption-albinism-stephanie-sinclair/|accessdate=11 December 2024|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20241105171823/https://time.com/longform/adoption-albinism-stephanie-sinclair/|archivedate=5 November 2024}}
# To put out of [[favor]]; to [[ruin]]; to [[label]] negatively.
#: {{ux|en|I’m afraid that if I speak out on this, I’ll be '''damned''' as a troublemaker.}}
# To condemn as [[unfit]], [[harmful]], [[invalid]], [[immoral]] or [[illegal]].
#: {{syn|en|anathematize|demonize|excoriate|vilify}}
#* '''1708''' November 8, {{w|Alexander Pope}}, letter to {{w|Henry Cromwell}}
#*: You are not so arrant a critic as to '''damn''' them [the works of modern poets] {{...}} without hearing.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=14 Feb 76|volume=3|number=33|journal=Gay Community News|page=11|title=Suicide|author=David Brill|text=Homosexuality and suicide have some common characteristics. Both are '''damned''' by the Western Judeo-Christian culture as sins (although the latter has only been considered such since the sixth century).}}
# {{lb|en|slang|slightly <<vulgar>>}} To [[curse]]; put a curse upon.
#: {{syn|en|comminate|execrate|imprecate}}
#: {{ux|en|That man stole my wallet. '''Damn''' him!}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} To invoke damnation; to curse.
#: {{syn|en|ban|execrate|point the bone}}
#* '''c. 1767-1774''', {{w|Oliver Goldsmith}}, ''letter to Mrs. Bunbury''
#*: {{...}} while I inwardly '''damn'''.

